Gibson Dunn is a leading global law firm, advising clients on significant transactions and disputes. Our exceptional teams craft and deploy creative legal strategies that are meticulously tailored to every matter, however complex or high-stakes. The firm’s work is distinguished by a unique combination of precision and vision.

Based in Washington D.C., the Law Student Recruiting Coordinator is responsible for coordinating all aspects of entry level hiring and on-campus marketing.

The Law Student Recruiting Coordinator will report to the Senior Manager, Law Student Recruiting. This role will also provide as-needed support to the Chief Recruiting Officer and the office’s local recruiting team.

**Responsibilities include:**

**U.S.-Wide Screening Interview Logistics & Coordination**

- Schedule and coordinate 2L screening interviews, OCI, and Early Interview Programs (EIP) across all offices;
- Coordinate with attorneys for interview participation and feedback collection;
- Funnel vetted candidates to local offices;
- Provide support to local offices for pre and post-offer in-person events (office receptions, super days).

**Law School Engagement**

- Plan, execute, and support pre-OCI outreach, including sponsorship coordination, event planning, and materials/swag preparation and delivery at all schools;
- Liaise with career services offices and student organizations;
- Manage school-specific calendars and communications;
- Develop firmwide recruiting marketing materials and/or campaigns to attract target candidates.

**Event Planning & Execution**

- Coordinate logistics for all in-person and virtual law school outreach events (e.g., receptions, info sessions, panels);
- Provide support to local offices for in-office outreach events (i.e. Home for the Holidays, Spring Reception);
- Manage attendee tracking and post-event follow-ups;
- Ensure firm branding and materials are current and consistent.

**Firmwide Training Support**

- Generate and coordinate enhanced firmwide summer program trainings;
- Participate in firmwide onboarding/integration projects, in coordination with professional development.

**Candidate Communication & Experience**

- Serve as a consistent point of contact for law student candidates throughout the process;
- Ensure timely responses to inquiries;
- Help maintain a positive and professional candidate experience aligned with our firm’s values.

**Data & Reporting**

- Enter and maintain candidate data in recruiting systems;
- Run reports and assist in post-season analysis and hiring metrics tracking;
- Support compliance with data privacy, NALP guidelines, and internal audit standards.

**Team & Operational Support**

- Create and maintain process documentation and timelines;
- Coordinate with marketing, diversity, and alumni relations teams where applicable;
- Provide support locally as needed.

**Qualifications:**

- Ideal candidate must have initiative and exhibit independent thinking and creativity.
- Excellent written and oral communication, organizational and interpersonal skills.
- The ability to work in a fast-paced environment, handle high volume, and juggle multiple projects and tasks

Mission

Akila is looking for an Technical Sales Manager to work with ambition, creativity, and a passion for building our Akila platform to transform and implement sustainability into facility management. The candidate should be comfortable working in a fast-moving startup environment where speed, hard work, and fresh thinking are critical to success

Key Responsibilities

- Identify Opportunities. Identify and optimize opportunities for business growth and development within the relevant business lines to offer the new solution to existing and new clients and promote expansion of the business.

- Provide technical pre-sale support & conduct pre-sales presentations and product demonstration if applicable, in support of Sales’ needs and requests.

- Request for Proposal (RFP) support: Evaluate criteria, coordinate support for entire response process, create deliverable metrics, identify timelines, and coordinate resources. Ensure client needs are met by proposal content; contribute to proposal writing as needed.

- Proposal delivery: QC, edit, and submit proposals as needed by sales, track status and send regular updates to team. Preparation of technical sales materials including collateral, quotation, timeline, project plan and solution proposals.

- Lead Proof of Concept (POC) activities with customers for our platform and set up projects team to ensure success of POC project.

- Proactively provide feedbacks to the Product and R&D and Commercial teams to drive the development and improvement of product direction and features based on customer experience and field observations.

Key Skills

- Solid network within the industry with a minimum of 8 years digital product presales & solution experience.

- Good knowledge on building management/automation system and operation or technical/computer science background.

- Excellent interpersonal skills and easy to connect and relate with. Able to “solution sell” with the ability to listen to your clients and understand what they really need rather than hard sell.

